The key condition is: $$
n \mid \frac{T(T+1)}{2} \quad \Leftrightarrow \quad T(T+1) \equiv 0 \pmod{2n}
$$

- If $ n $ is **not** a power of two, then there exist coprime factors $ a, b $ of $ 2n $ such that the solution $ T $ to the system: $$
  T \equiv 0 \pmod{a}, \quad T \equiv -1 \pmod{b}
  $$

$$
\boxed{\text{All natural numbers except the powers of two}}
$$
